<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n71932" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄβρῐμος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, also
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>Or.</u>
			1454
		</span></i> (lyr.) :—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>strong, mighty,</i> epith. of Ares, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.845
			</span></i>, al. ; of Achilles, <i><span class="en">
				19.408
			</span></i> ; of Hector, <i><span class="en">
				8.473
			</span></i> ; also of things, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄ. ἔγχος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					3.357
				</span></i>
			, etc. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄχθος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					9.233
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυρεός, λίθος,</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				241
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				305
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδωρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					4.453
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐβρόντησε ὄβριμον</span> he
			thundered <i>mightily,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				839
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄ. ἔργα</span> deeds <i>of
				might,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Tyrt.
				11.27
			</span></i>.—
				Ep.
			 word, rare in Trag., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνδρες ὄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					794
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῖσος ὄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1411
				</span></i>
			(lyr.) ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰδαία μᾶτερ ὀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
				</span></i>
			 l. c. —The form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμβριμος</span> is a freq. f.l., as in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.845
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				4.8
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				<u>P.</u>
				9.27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
			</span></i>l. c. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βριμός: μέγας, χαλεπός,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, to which <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄβριμος</span> may be
			related as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀβριμώ <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῑ]</span></span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				698
			</span></i> to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βριμώ, Ὀβριαρεύς</span> to
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βριαρεύς,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				346.41
			</span></i>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀβριάρεως</span> to
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βριάρεως</span> ; cf. also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βρίμη, βριμάομαι, βριαρός.</span>)</div>
